Introduction
Recruiting the right talent can be a time-consuming and challenging task. CV Matcher simplifies this process by providing an intelligent system that compares candidate CVs against job descriptions or predefined requirements. This project is ideal for HR teams, recruiters, and organizations looking to automate their hiring pipelines.

Key Objectives:
Automate CV matching to save time and resources.
Increase the accuracy of candidate-job matching using machine learning.
Provide detailed insights and scoring for each match.
Features
Automated CV Parsing: Extracts key information from CVs such as skills, experience, and education.
Job Description Analysis: Breaks down job descriptions into structured, comparable data points.
Matching Algorithm: Matches CVs to job descriptions using natural language processing (NLP) techniques.
Scoring System: Provides a compatibility score for each CV-job pairing.
Interactive Dashboard: Visualize results and dig into the details of each match.
Customizable Criteria: Tailor the matching algorithm to your organization's needs.
Installation
Follow these steps to get started with CV Matcher:

Clone the Repository:

bash
git clone https://github.com/humeniucDan/CV-Matcher.git
cd CV-Matcher
Set Up the Environment: Install the required Python dependencies in a virtual environment:

bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows use `venv\Scripts\activate`
pip install -r requirements.txt
Run the Application: Execute the main script to start the application:

bash
python app.py
Optional: Set up a Jupyter Notebook environment for experimentation:

bash
jupyter notebook
Usage
Upload candidate CVs in supported formats (e.g., PDF, DOCX).
Provide a job description or set of criteria for comparison.
Run the matching algorithm to generate scores and insights.
Review results via the interactive dashboard or exported reports.
