Throughput Process
The Throughput Process outlines the flow of information and operations within the CV Matcher system:

Input Phase:

Upload CVs in PDF or DOCX formats.
Provide job descriptions or other criteria for matching.
Parsing Phase:

CVs are parsed to extract key fields such as:
Name
Contact Details
Skills
Work Experience
Education
Job descriptions are analyzed to identify required skills, qualifications, and experience.
Data Preprocessing:

Remove unnecessary data, standardize text formats, and tokenize content.
Convert text to numerical representations using NLP techniques (e.g., TF-IDF, word embeddings).
Matching Phase:

Compare CV data with job description data using the matching algorithm.
Calculate compatibility scores based on:
Skill overlap
Experience relevance
Education match
Keywords and semantic similarity.
Scoring and Insights:

Generate scores for each CV-job pairing.
Provide insights into strengths and weaknesses of each match.
Output Phase:

Present results in an interactive dashboard.
Export reports for further analysis or sharing with stakeholders.
