FAQ and Questions
Below are key questions about the project that need to be addressed:

Why was this project created?
The project was created to automate and improve the process of matching CVs to job descriptions, reducing manual effort and increasing hiring efficiency.

How does the matching algorithm work?
The algorithm uses natural language processing (NLP) techniques to analyze and compare text data from CVs and job descriptions. It assigns scores based on keyword matching, semantic similarity, and other customizable criteria.

What are the main use cases for this tool?
Recruitment automation for HR teams.
Candidate-job matching for staffing agencies.
Educational or training programs looking to assess candidate readiness.
How can I customize the criteria for matching?
You can modify the algorithm's parameters or provide a configuration file specifying custom weights for skills, experience, or other factors.

What file formats are supported for CV uploads?
Currently, the tool supports PDF and DOCX formats. Additional formats can be added with minimal effort.

How can I contribute to the development of the project?
See the Contributing section for detailed steps on how to get involved.

